          "text": {
            "description1": "KACHALU (Jazirat Abu Sufur): this is a small island located straight north away from the Musandam Peninsula. It is a great combination of walls and slopes with beautiful hard and soft coral gardens. Depth: 10–40 meters. REMARKS: There is always strong current in the area!",
            "description2": "Giant Trevally, Pinjalo, Jackfish, Snappers, Sweet-lips, King and Batfish, Lobster, even Eagle rays and Stingrays. If you’re lucky: Hammerheads, White-tip sharks, and Mola-Mola."
          },
